{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/701700-speak-friend-and-enter","id":701700,"title":"Speak friend and enter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-14T23:12:19-07:00","id":701700,"title":"Speak friend and enter","content":"I need ideas. In my current chronicle my heroes need to find out what lies beyond a sealed door at the end of an abandoned trod never meant to be opened again. The door was sealed by the Lost using a contract so I figure the most likely way to open it is by using its 'catch', a condition that if met will release the locks and allow the door to open. Problem is coming up with a 'catch', any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T00:24:02-07:00","id":701775,"title":"","content":"It contains the remaining copies of the Atari E.T game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-15-2015, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T03:25:21-07:00","id":701888,"title":"","content":"Any reason why the Trod was closed? In this sort of thing, context can be important.<br /> <br /> But, devoid of that, I'd say someone has to burn their hand and then press their still warm wound onto the door itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T07:37:56-07:00","id":702074,"title":"","content":"It could only be opened by the infamous token Hand of Glory. Usually it is made from hand of a murderer that was hanged on midnight. Common catches are either some health damage to the user or murderous possession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T11:39:52-07:00","id":702377,"title":"","content":"If whoever sealed it never intended it be opened again, the catch is likely something that is possible, but extremely difficult to figure out and convoluted. For example, you need to dab a tear collected in March from a man between 18 and 20 whose new business had just collapsed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T12:55:51-07:00","id":702447,"title":"","content":"Why not go the opposite way... why have them open it to find out what is behind it when it could make things both more interesting and dire if it was slowly opening on its own. Now they have to discover what was sealed behind the door and how/why it was sealed in the first place before it opens... and what might be causing it to open now when it has been sealed for decades. Perhaps they are all experiencing dreams that draw them to this particular trod because the door that was to remain closed is opening once more... is this a defense to warn the Lost of something... or the influence of whatever is on the other side of the door? What if those they need help from suspect that the players are the ones trying to open it... or they are trying to open it to right something they did all those years ago themselves. Maybe the cost of closing/sealing the door is a heavy price to pay... one that only the most steel-willed changelings can even hope to pay... even at the cost of their own Clarity. So many delicious questions... each with its own savory answer to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T09:00:57-07:00","id":703519,"title":"","content":"Another &quot;creative&quot; option: Ignore the door and go through the wall (if that kind of twist moves the story in the right way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T09:27:04-07:00","id":703588,"title":"","content":"Have the players tried removing the screws from the hinges? Technically the door isn't opened, it's just been moved from its fixed position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T02:40:52-07:00","id":704571,"title":"","content":"Opposing forces working together? Its a classic idea - two individuals with dramatically opposing goals/morals/ideologies, who shouldn't even be in the same room together without bloodshed. Remember the portal to the Abyss (in Dragonlance)? Open-able only by a Black Robe (evil mage) and good priest working in tandem?<br /> <br /> Now, that would have to be adapted, of course. So how about making it so a changeling and his fetch both have to turn the knob at the same time?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Oh, and keep in mind that the fae are the ultimate rules-lawyers. So they almost certainly built a loophole in for their own use. <i>Sure, its sealed &quot;forever&quot; . . . you can trust us </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 10-17-2015, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T01:47:41-07:00","id":708417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Retias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/701700-speak-friend-and-enter?p=702377#post702377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If whoever sealed it never intended it be opened again, the catch is likely something that is possible, but extremely difficult to figure out and convoluted. For example, you need to dab a tear collected in March from a man between 18 and 20 whose new business had just collapsed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I have always assumed that the catch is never something the Fae consciously add to their work. It is something that unconsciously happens mostly due to their connection with the Wyrd. As a result the catch might be obscure, but it is always connected to the story at hand. The catch needs to make sense in some fashion. Even if there is no such connection with the Wyrd, making it a random weakness makes it impossible for the PCs to learn and how is the story served by that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So my counter question would be: What is behind the door? What is the story about the door? For example, if something is locked up that is related to darkness, the weakness might be the first sun rays of the midsummer sun or when it was a dragon with a love for maidens the kiss of one in love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}